    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-10-06; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Alert, warm, and witty; weight 80.4 kg, BMI 25.4. Each step of the examination described to him before it was done</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Dark glasses removed with his permission. No light perception. Lids and ocular surfaces quiet, with no redness, swelling, or discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Canals and tympanic membranes normal; whispered voice heard on both sides</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>No thyroid enlargement or nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Regular rhythm at 68 per minute; no murmur; no edema</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Clear to auscultation bilaterally</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft and non-tender; no masses or organ enlargement</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>No suspicious lesions</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Timed Up and Go 10 seconds, walking independently after a spoken orientation to the room; steady gait</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Fluent conversation; recalled three of three words after a delay; no focal deficit. Cognitive function assessed by direct observation and a verbal recall task, because the clock-drawing part of the Mini-Cog is not valid for a blind patient</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Euthymic; judgment and insight intact</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

