  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed, personalized prevention plan updated, and a written copy sent as an accessible electronic document. Depression, alcohol, and drug-use screens are negative. No cognitive concern. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is about 13 percent by the pooled cohort equations, driven by age, with no diabetes, hypertension, dyslipidemia, or smoking. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Opioid use disorder, in sustained remission (F11.21)</content>. Sustained remission continues. Naloxone is in date, and the plan for any future pain is on file. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in his phone. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item><item>Replace the naloxone before its expiry date.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Blindness of both eyes since childhood (H54.0X55)</content>. Eyes comfortable and quiet, as at the ophthalmology examination in the spring. [S]<list><item>Yearly ophthalmology review in the spring; same-day review for eye pain or redness.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; none on record</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Two-dose series recommended; first dose at the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at 65 and older; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No dose on record in the past ten years; with the first zoster dose</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 75 and older, and from 50 with conditions that raise risk, which he does not have; review yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0, read aloud; PHQ-9 2 at the six-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2, below the risk threshold, read aloud</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>DAST-10 score 0 for the past year, read aloud; sustained remission</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C, hepatitis B, and HIV testing</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Recommended once for all adults and for people with a past substance use disorder; no prior result on record; drawn today with his consent, and results to be sent to him in an accessible format</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Direct observation and a verbal three-word recall (3 of 3); the clock-drawing task is not used for a blind patient</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 10 seconds; home layout kept fixed; sighted guide in unfamiliar places</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No concern; whispered voice heard on both sides. Hearing is his main way of finding his way, so any change should be checked promptly</td></tr><tr><td>Vision and eye care</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Blind since childhood; ophthalmology examination in the spring; yearly review</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>126/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>LDL 110 mg/dL at intake. Ten-year risk about 13 percent, but with no diabetes, hypertension, dyslipidemia, or smoking the criteria for a statin are not met; discussed, and he chose not to start one; revisit yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.5 percent at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No prior screening on record. He chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test; the kit&apos;s instructions were given as an audio file and the kit has tactile markers. A positive test needs colonoscopy</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision-making about the small benefit and the risks of overdiagnosis; he chose not to have PSA testing</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No tobacco use on record</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, glaucoma and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Chronic-care review in three months, with the first zoster dose and the Tdap booster. Test results sent to him as accessible electronic messages. Yearly ophthalmology review in the spring. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent. He named a health care agent, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. The form was read aloud to him in full before he signed it, and he was given an accessible electronic copy. He said that what matters most to him is staying independent, keeping up his work, and protecting his recovery, and that he wants to be asked directly, not through others, about any medicine that could affect it. He chose not to record specific treatment preferences today. The plan will be revisited yearly or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
